---
title: Chapter 8: Decision Modelling, Simulation, and the Value of Information
---
flowchart TD
 S1["1. Translate the decision into a model specification\nDefine the causal structure, states or events, time horizon, perspective, outputs, and decision rule."]
 S2["2. Select the analytic or simulation method\nMatch decision tree, Markov, microsimulation, discrete-event, system-dynamics, agent-based, or hybrid methods to the problem."]
 S1 --> S2
 S3["3. Assemble data, parameters, and evidence\nDocument sources, distributions, correlations, assumptions, heterogeneity, and versions."]
 S2 --> S3
 S4["4. Implement and verify\nTest logic, calculations, traces, extreme values, convergence, and code or spreadsheet integrity."]
 S3 --> S4
 S5["5. Validate for the intended use\nAssess face, internal, external, predictive, and decision validity proportionately."]
 S4 --> S5
 S6["6. Characterize uncertainty and value of information\nTest parameter, structural, methodological, and scenario uncertainty and identify valuable additional evidence."]
 S5 --> S6
 S7["7. Communicate and archive\nPresent disaggregated results, decision uncertainty, limitations, reproducibility, and versioned records."]
 S6 --> S7
 classDef process fill:#fff,stroke:#7A1730,stroke-width:2px,color:#222
 class S1,S2,S3,S4,S5,S6,S7,S8,S9,S10 process
